  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian response for internally displaced persons and returnees with protection needs in HondurasHumanitarian response for internally displaced persons and returnees with protection needs in Honduras</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The 2025 Humanitarian Needs and Response Plan (HNRP) prioritize three shocks: violence, mixed movements, and climate-related events like storms, floods, and droughts, requiring a coordinated response. As protection risks continue to grow, gender-based violence remains a daily threat, the escalation of territorial conflicts heightens risks for human rights defenders and rural communities, and more Hondurans face threats to their lives, integrity or liberty. Additionally, the 2025 electoral process further heightens the risk profiles of vulnerable populations, exacerbating the context. In response to this context, and in line with the HNRP 2025 priorities, under this proposal, IOM proposes an inclusive strategic protection approach to improve and scale up the humanitarian response in affected communities, reception and shelter centres.</narrative>
  </description>
